    "instructions": "You are identifying every visible line and scatter series in a cropped chart.\nMultiple plot panels or small multiples are supported. Treat each visible panel as part of the same chart run.\nDistinguish panels using clear location language such as top-left panel, right panel, lower panel, or panel title.\nWhen naming axes or series in a multi-panel chart, include enough panel context in axis_id, location_description, series_name, or visual_description to avoid ambiguity.\n\nIdentify all line and scatter series in every visible panel. Do not stop after five or any other arbitrary count.\nClassify a series as line when its data is visibly connected, including lines that also have markers. Classify unconnected data markers as scatter. A fitted or reference line over scatter data is a separate line series.\nFor each series, provide its name, series_type, colour, line style, marker style, estimated point count, and visual description.\nThe line_color value must be either a Pillow named colour accepted by PIL.ImageColor, such as red, blue, darkgreen, or lightgray, or a hex colour such as #2563eb. Do not use informal colour descriptions that Pillow cannot parse.\nUse marker_style to describe scatter marker shape and fill, such as filled circle, hollow square, diamond, triangle, plus, or x. It may be null for a line without relevant markers.\nSet estimated_total_points to the number of individually visible scatter markers. It may be null for line series.\nAlso identify which available x-axis and y-axis applies to each series using the provided axis_id values.\nUse the legend, labels, panel titles, line appearance, markers, and visual position to distinguish series.\nDo not return point coordinates in this step.\nIdentify unsupported conditions: unsupported chart content, logarithmic axes, categorical axes, broken axes, unreadable labels, or charts where the requested line or scatter data cannot be visually traced.\nIf such a condition is present, return